Webviews (extension details pages, Markdown preview, extension panels) come
from this server, not from Microsoft's vscode-cdn.net. The browser client
otherwise loads them from product.json's webviewContentExternalBaseUrlTemplate,
which on VSCodium points to an old Microsoft build on the CDN: its service
worker does not match this client ("Found unexpected service worker version.
Found: 4. Expected: 6") and the pages stay empty; offline they cannot load at
all.

- webClientServer.ts: the server passes webviewEndpoint, the webview files under
  its own /static route.
- environmentService.ts: the client makes that path absolute (the webview code
  needs the endpoint's origin).
- pre/index.html: a webview served from the workbench's own origin cannot carry
  the per-webview hostname that index.html checks, so the same origin is
  accepted; the CSP hash of the inline script is updated to match.
  As code-server does; the webviews then share the workbench's origin, which
  suits this per-user server on 127.0.0.1.

Could go upstream (microsoft/vscode, as an option of the server's web client).

--- a/src/vs/server/node/webClientServer.ts
+++ b/src/vs/server/node/webClientServer.ts
@@ -424,7 +424,10 @@
 			folderUri: resolveWorkspaceURI(this._environmentService.args['default-folder']),
 			workspaceUri: resolveWorkspaceURI(this._environmentService.args['default-workspace']),
 			productConfiguration,
-			callbackRoute: callbackRoute
+			callbackRoute: callbackRoute,
+			// Webviews from this server, not from Microsoft's vscode-cdn.net, which
+			// has only Microsoft's own builds (commits).
+			webviewEndpoint: posix.join(staticRoute, 'out/vs/workbench/contrib/webview/browser/pre')
 		};
 
 		const cookies = cookie.parse(req.headers.cookie || '');
--- a/src/vs/workbench/contrib/webview/browser/pre/index.html
+++ b/src/vs/workbench/contrib/webview/browser/pre/index.html
@@ -5,7 +5,7 @@
 	<meta charset="UTF-8">
 
 	<meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy"
-		content="default-src 'none'; script-src 'sha256-7cKy9iQfWRXcgRS74x6I4q5cRDkv8nQz51jecqMmQ5w=' 'self'; frame-src 'self'; style-src 'unsafe-inline';">
+		content="default-src 'none'; script-src 'sha256-Zzp95sw2ShG1XGhmLXU+xzK8GCXE5mPIvsHOiW5CCHo=' 'self'; frame-src 'self'; style-src 'unsafe-inline';">
 
 	<!-- Disable pinch zooming -->
 	<meta name="viewport"
@@ -345,6 +345,12 @@
 
 				const hostname = location.hostname;
 
+				// Served by the workbench's own server (vscode-server's webviewEndpoint):
+				// the same origin cannot carry the per-webview hostname checked below.
+				if (parentOrigin === location.origin) {
+					return start(parentOrigin);
+				}
+
 				if (!crypto.subtle) {
 					// cannot validate, not running in a secure context
 					throw new Error(`'crypto.subtle' is not available so webviews will not work. This is likely because the editor is not running in a secure context (https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Security/Secure_Contexts).`);
--- a/src/vs/workbench/services/environment/browser/environmentService.ts
